    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="1292" n="1178" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister Churchill
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d539-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hyde
                                Park</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-26"
                            >August 26, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From the President to Colonel Warden, Personal and Secret. Number 347. I hope you
                    have seen Uncle Joe’s new message<anchor n="2" xml:id="d539-f2"/> which is <pb
                        facs="1293" n="1179" xml:id="pg1179"/> greatly improved in its tone. As you
                    and he know, I am lost until Monday and I would let a few days go by till we
                    answer him.</p>
                <p>However, my first feeling is that he has come around to our secondary meeting and
                    that it should be held very soon.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d539-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d539-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the White House Map Room and the British Admiralty Delegation at
                    Washington. Churchill was in Canada at this time.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d539-f2" n="2" xml:id="d539-f2-content">
                <p>i.e., Stalin’s message of August 24, 1943, which had just reached Roosevelt at
                    Hyde Park. See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1174">p.
                        1174</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
